    "Description": "This distribution provides a Perl interface to allow reading and writing of compressed data created with the zlib and bzip2 libraries.  IO-Compress supports reading and writing of bzip2, RFC 1950, RFC 1951, RFC 1952 (i.e. gzip) and zip files/buffers.  The following modules used to be distributed separately, but are now included with the IO-Compress distribution:\n* Compress-Zlib\n* IO-Compress-Zlib\n* IO-Compress-Bzip2\n* IO-Compress-Base\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* perl-IO-Compress: perl-IO-Compress: Arbitrary code execution via attacker-controlled output glob (CVE-2026-48962)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
